<title>USA: ContiFinancial sells $200 mln senior notes.</title>
<headline>ContiFinancial sells $200 mln senior notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>ContiFinancial Corp said on Monday it sold $200 million in senior notes maturing March 15, 2002, with a 7.5 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The notes, which are not subject to redemption prior to maturity, were initially bought by Bearn Stearns &amp; Co and Credit Suisse First Boston Corp for placement with institutional investors.</p>
<p>The proceeds will be used to prepay notes to ContiFinancial's majority stockholder, Continental Grain Co.</p>
<p>ContiFinancial is a consumer and commercial finance company.</p>
</text>
